  "result": "I added `formatBytes(n)` in `src/cli/bytes.ts` and committed it as `f2d89f9`.\n\nIt returns B, KiB, MiB or GiB with one decimal, for example `1536` gives `1.5 KiB`. Values of 1024 GiB or more stay in GiB. Negative numbers keep their sign, so `-2048` gives `-2.0 KiB`. A value that rounds up to 1024 moves to the next unit, so it shows `1.0 KiB` rather than `1024.0 B`.\n\nThe tests are in `test/cli/bytes.test.ts` and cover each unit, the unit boundaries and negatives. The two tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` is clean, and biome reports no problems on the two new files. I didn't run the full `npm run gate`.",
